<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia reduces Minas crude exports in August.</title>
<headline>Indonesia reduces Minas crude exports in August.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian state oil company Pertamina has reduced its August allocations of Minas crude by 27 percent from July to just 38,000 barrels-per-day(bpd), industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Traders said the cut in Minas was due preparations to start-up the 65,000-bpd crude distillation unit (CDU) at the Balikpapan refinery, scheduled to come onstream in August.</p>
<p>Indonesia allocated Arun crude for the first time since May.</p>
<p>Traders said a delay in the test runs at Indonesia's Humpuss condensate splitter had led to the availability of Arun.  </p>
<p>The splitter was due to have test runs in mid June, but was delayed to end July.</p>
<p>Industry sources said Pertamina made the following allocations: (Figures are in barrels per day)</p>
<p>	    August  July	June	May</p>
<p>MINAS     38,000  52,000    62,000    73,000</p>
<p>DURI	31,000  20,000    33,000    60,000</p>
<p>WIDURI    48,000  17,000    28,000    18,000</p>
<p>CINTA     35,000  17,000     4,000    14,000</p>
<p>ARUN	20,000   none	 none    24,000</p>
<p>BELIDA    15,000  30,000     6,000    10,000</p>
<p>B. MIX    35,000  28,000    18,000    35,000</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3082)</p>
